From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 22:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(llama-cpp): rank with nvidia/llama-nemotron-rerank-1b-v2

Carried as a llama.cpp patch beside the others
(patches/0010-llama-nemotron-rerank.patch), ported from ggml-org/llama.cpp#24083
(open) onto our pin ddf48f8: the converter registers
LlamaBidirectionalForSequenceClassification (bidirectional Llama 3.2 1B, the
last hidden states mean-pooled, a `score` head giving a raw logit) with causal
attention off, pooling RANK, classifier pooling MEAN, the model's rerank
template and score.weight as cls.output; llama-embed loads the optional head;
the server gives a rerank template's prompt the BOS its tokenizer adds. This
base already pools before the head when the GGUF says classifier pooling mean
(the ModernBERT gte path), so no graph change.

STAGED for a separate backend used only by the reranker benchmark's arm A3
(the operator, 2026-11-10: "Patch llama.cpp to support nemo reranker,
tomorrow I want to see its benchmarks too"); it enters the live series only
if that arm earns it, so no live engine changes for it.

Assisted-by: Claude Code
